#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119512 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "fe3edf12-af5b-5bb0-b5b3-efb6cd809134" :question/math-academy-id "e-4394" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/assets/fc2ed708d717844ca73b7ecbfd8467923fad091ae524153350e7e2fb3df1ea4e.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/assets/5260137f2dbf20b44400659be8467da333ff228e5bff323465f920a9505ee5f2.png)\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: $a_{21}=6 \\neq 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119513 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "d7c263d4-5d0a-52cd-b876-cfa3bd3171e0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4395" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are lower triangular matrices?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/assets/ad9636de9b8c93338350a6b99d88476b481ed1bf03a5dd64935abedbdb626524.png)" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is a lower triangular matrix since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $A$ and $C$ are *not* lower triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23} & =1\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{13} & =1\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119525 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "205d32a2-ac26-5eaf-896a-c6182a70eff7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4498" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/assets/4dd9b1c1b3d789c166ecd8f6d2a909609c7f4324705c84115cce84a29181bf32.png)\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular\n\n- $A^T-A$ is lower triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/assets/c1ec838cd30cca8fbb2e3996d5a7d84dadb233e1951d05b532a9d606d887eb2f.png)\n\n- Statement II is true, since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/assets/f39c68a9b1f5e16caffbf159b629a958e147e14099334b049bdfcd857eef84d2.png)\n\n- Statement III is false, since the result of $A^T-A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075464/assets/f4415c87201f5b92f23e3320c313cd58ac4e720135928645896f976614c5eaa0.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "590bb304-862a-588b-bb15-df145c6f825d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382791} {:answer/id #uuid "411061f1-f1cc-56b3-8a5a-f0b772f62390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382792} {:answer/id #uuid "888ba710-2c97-5cc8-b27a-c514b7b87333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382793} {:answer/id #uuid "7031e379-d5cb-5f90-b692-1a9d54b3261c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382794} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a8b60a-363c-56bd-862f-693f032d99f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "888ba710-2c97-5cc8-b27a-c514b7b87333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382793} :answer-field/id #uuid "327dd9a6-0517-54c4-ab7f-6828b341ad87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f565581c-3596-5b33-9191-b3b143b96ba2" :question/math-academy-id "q-126340" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${c}_{21}=-5\\ne 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baa67f3b-871a-5885-af13-63f8075fb710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382798} {:answer/id #uuid "665dfc3f-2d68-53be-8d8a-32186f5edced" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382799} {:answer/id #uuid "bad6cecb-8db4-57ef-a451-2e1ee485e3dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382800} {:answer/id #uuid "43d4f24e-7211-5f76-8d4b-33380c3ec4f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382801} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ce9b52-6381-5315-875e-ac971b088c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2ce9b52-6381-5315-875e-ac971b088c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382802} :answer-field/id #uuid "46487577-cacf-5e81-b9a4-2c774b716a1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e0ae1a7-d37b-5c56-b70b-849175c97c12" :question/math-academy-id "q-126342" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is an upper triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not a lower triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element above the diagonal: ${c}_{12}=1\\ne 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eda78f6b-3a7d-5366-8e9e-1f9faa88236c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382805} {:answer/id #uuid "b647786d-9d31-5477-9cfc-f7e5838d972c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$, $B$, and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382806} {:answer/id #uuid "2494b0ea-1a3d-51bd-a30c-f9f3fe8101a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382807} {:answer/id #uuid "bec23df0-1c46-5546-98ec-caa0c70223ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382808} {:answer/id #uuid "a52954b6-41ab-5cee-97b7-fc8482f2960e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2494b0ea-1a3d-51bd-a30c-f9f3fe8101a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382807} :answer-field/id #uuid "88e773c8-4076-5d11-b4d4-a49a4229cb82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0957d41c-269e-58e7-a417-3e81fdfb9faf" :question/math-academy-id "q-126351" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are lower triangular matrices?\n\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The matrices $A$ and $B$ are lower triangular matrices since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrix $C$ is *not* a lower triangular matrix since it has a non-zero element above the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =-2\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382810 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "938b0f8f-2c07-504a-91ac-eba22105ddbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382812} {:answer/id #uuid "00ead7cc-e5b5-58c6-8d80-9b9234bc6e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382813} {:answer/id #uuid "4db657c0-6802-5830-8da9-41b5cb9a5db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382814} {:answer/id #uuid "621da94f-244a-550e-a0c9-7c63aa7c796b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382815} {:answer/id #uuid "4fd92f11-ddca-59b6-80a7-01d7e8969599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "621da94f-244a-550e-a0c9-7c63aa7c796b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382815} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c82e418-eee7-55cc-8944-b47e0ba42402" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3cca3ca2-ad9e-5a68-b3d3-231d7c0b3f2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-126352" :question/problem "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "750e4b45-c8f4-51b4-8d8f-01f572fb38dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310106} {:answer/id #uuid "6cc29a43-154c-5465-aa36-fdc614511403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310107} {:answer/id #uuid "1f651fce-89b8-51ab-be6d-321c867e43ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310108} {:answer/id #uuid "1c71c9ee-de90-5e1f-a983-dbc831d74c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310109} {:answer/id #uuid "51ee84c1-5afe-5255-95cd-1f857e719a6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "750e4b45-c8f4-51b4-8d8f-01f572fb38dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310106} :answer-field/id #uuid "56cdfa8b-979f-516b-9333-9e91c1bcda79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ada2c6aa-e1cf-5c5d-97a8-778452c8133f" :question/math-academy-id "q-126479" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $C$ is upper triangular\n- $C$ is lower triangular\n- ${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of $C$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $C$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${C}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120045 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a44b5058-f144-5b6a-b278-d37709c24ab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116836} {:answer/id #uuid "a467653a-414d-5b69-930e-ddc2ab9ae250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116837} {:answer/id #uuid "e95757b7-75fc-5952-88e3-dc6d206d6640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116838} {:answer/id #uuid "2d709ef2-dee7-5bb2-a018-15cfe40e0232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116839} {:answer/id #uuid "663a032b-d529-58a1-a8d2-b550fb315588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a467653a-414d-5b69-930e-ddc2ab9ae250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116837} :answer-field/id #uuid "514e70b3-6303-5301-bfda-6e0070e42283" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6f9badf-44cd-56b4-946a-abae3220a5b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-13759" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${a}_{21}=3\\ne 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe5353e1-a225-5101-bf32-1c0fdfbc64bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310120} {:answer/id #uuid "3d047da7-3d95-5b64-a0c6-d853b655d76f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310121} {:answer/id #uuid "dad18cef-425c-50d3-bae2-2e2b955ad092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310122} {:answer/id #uuid "dbab06e0-5c33-5e18-9c15-041b4443f17a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310123} {:answer/id #uuid "5a34fb66-8d4f-5071-967c-0421912d882e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a34fb66-8d4f-5071-967c-0421912d882e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310124} :answer-field/id #uuid "556dd9f0-f531-576f-aa1b-2afbb468aaee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "817df60a-a122-5c88-a4b8-f32eff3f52e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-13760" :question/problem "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de7d0245-96b7-5a2e-aff7-d0a92b57972a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382819} {:answer/id #uuid "4ebd4a1b-1207-53c4-ae88-67f21abc2a88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382820} {:answer/id #uuid "a16117b0-08a0-5f82-94dc-3e288879c3a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382821} {:answer/id #uuid "f015fd8c-9853-570f-83f1-3f3c7526f7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382822} {:answer/id #uuid "88dbe141-0237-5ebd-8005-762fa964b7da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de7d0245-96b7-5a2e-aff7-d0a92b57972a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382819} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f6e1c2d-7baf-5e31-8a72-553208a7be7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c98606c5-5ad1-5a44-8d53-a6f6cf880ec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-13771" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular\n- $A$ is lower triangular\n- ${A}^{T}+A$ is lower triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true, since the result of $A+{A}^{T}$ has all the entries above the main diagonal equal to zero: \n\n$$\n{A}^{T}+A=[\\begin{aligned}16 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ae6a9a-903f-5067-b94c-f6e970a0f366" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382826} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9233ca-f2b3-53ca-8426-d9b30ce1f43c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382827} {:answer/id #uuid "036df1ec-0c6f-5b48-8950-6294019bb986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382828} {:answer/id #uuid "ff871c76-2229-5cc9-8790-ec48f62abb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382829} {:answer/id #uuid "810a9d4c-0007-5715-ac35-045ec8606d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff871c76-2229-5cc9-8790-ec48f62abb92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382829} :answer-field/id #uuid "84349fe5-adb7-535d-a9da-fd45d503f01a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfcf7437-e2f1-55f7-9a36-7baaca570fc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-13779" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above and below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a diagonal matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c348ec0d-ec14-5ab3-b31b-62c45b43c86b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118564} {:answer/id #uuid "f799ec7b-3561-5729-a81c-88e3d3e97416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118565} {:answer/id #uuid "2953424a-c761-5832-bf1c-5ad1e817b628" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118566} {:answer/id #uuid "6838e181-7f7b-53d2-beaa-db8004fec2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118567} {:answer/id #uuid "7d7c341f-ecc1-5d20-bddd-1103016b4f25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d7c341f-ecc1-5d20-bddd-1103016b4f25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118568} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9c79ad-5239-5ddd-bf74-1e3f8db763bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a1fe1df-e314-527e-a884-f0c092b97472" :question/math-academy-id "q-42090" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 11\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =5\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =3\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dfd8f6d-e020-5293-a845-5b2f764f47b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118570} {:answer/id #uuid "c071b3a1-dbaf-5718-8f17-9bd8ae571705" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118571} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd547a4-9472-5339-ad66-accf99890902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118572} {:answer/id #uuid "765e4fb8-8a9a-55d5-88ab-31b36ee7537e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118573} {:answer/id #uuid "783db2f5-492b-5b95-974b-ab65afca4929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "783db2f5-492b-5b95-974b-ab65afca4929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118574} :answer-field/id #uuid "096b89f4-2931-59a2-8b85-9c15b72fecaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39d12d09-6555-5993-ad4c-5e191be1b0c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-42091" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular\n- $A$ is lower triangular\n- ${A}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $A$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${A}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6a1aaec-41fe-5805-9aca-2d7bb008d178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382833} {:answer/id #uuid "b0295ed6-c38f-551a-a0c5-83dc246ea592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382834} {:answer/id #uuid "2b61ea15-7ad6-5d32-a0ed-65d03e42969f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382835} {:answer/id #uuid "a9fb7c3e-f8c3-5c25-94fc-74af0e5c0b27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382836} {:answer/id #uuid "d0effccf-e3cb-51f9-965d-e942f84fe48c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0295ed6-c38f-551a-a0c5-83dc246ea592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382834} :answer-field/id #uuid "588d5705-43ea-5d79-be22-88fac1741406" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4ace65b7-bf81-524d-8427-a694b672af28" :question/math-academy-id "q-42116" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular\n- ${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular\n- $A$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since the result of ${A}^{T}-A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}-A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310153 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d05f5a6a-bf6c-5d84-bcdc-d9368c9cbef8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310155} {:an